<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CBA says rate cuts boost housing.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CBA says rate cuts boost housing.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Bank of Australia said on Tuesday that recent cuts in official interest rates and its own cuts to variable home loan rates had triggered an increase in a demand for home loans across the financial system.</p>
<p>&quot;The latest reduction in interest rates and the changes that we made in interest rates have served to improve affordability and that's shown through in increased demand for home loans across the system,&quot; CBA managing director David Murray told reporters after the bank's annual meeting in Melbourne.</p>
</text>
